# Findings the image scan should stay quiet about, with the reason and the
# condition for looking again. Nothing goes in here to make a red mark green:
# if a line cannot say why, the finding gets fixed instead.
#
# Both entries below come from the same place: pip vendors its own dependencies
# and lists them in pip/_vendor/vendor.txt, which Trivy reads as if those were
# installed packages. They are not Evermind's dependencies, the container never
# runs pip, and there is nothing on our side to upgrade.

# msgpack 1.1.2, high. Vendored inside pip, where it deserialises pip's own HTTP
# cache. Every released pip up to 26.2.1 still vendors 1.1.2; only pip's main
# branch has moved to the fixed 1.2.1.
# Remove once a pip release ships msgpack >= 1.2.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools 70.3.0, high. Read from that same vendor.txt, and this one is not
# even present: there is no pip/_vendor/setuptools directory in the image, and
# before 2.0.5 setuptools was not installed at all. The line in vendor.txt is
# all Trivy is seeing.
# Remove once pip's vendor.txt names setuptools >= 78.1.1, or stops naming it.
CVE-2025-47273
